            <ArticleTitle>Untreated pain, narcotics regulation, and global health ideologies.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e1001411</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1371/journal.pmed.1001411</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain management is marginalized or ignored, with millions of people worldwide unnecessarily living with untreated pain. Reducing global inequalities in untreated pain requires a concerted global effort, say Veronique Fraser and colleagues, which must attend to the complexity of pain and promote multimodal, multidisciplinary pain management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
